From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:50:22 -0400
Subject: [M156] [SkSL] Reject invalid types when parsing

Original change's description:
> [SkSL] Reject invalid types when parsing
>
> When parsing runtime effects, we alias private types to fInvalid to
> ensure they are not used or referenced as variable names. This ensures
> we emit errors for those types anywhere they are encountered, moving the
> check from variable declarations to the parser.
>
> Bug: 574213633
> Change-Id: I6a27aead1ed83315e137752c5ef124e2f2020df4
> Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1400318
> Commit-Queue: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>
> Reviewed-by: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>

